{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793451146,"nonce":"TWW2aL4+3uLhSqcFglftCeWIBDk=","message":"Agent platform plan (darmie's direction, consolidated by rayde-00)\n\nDecided\n- nan8 is the control plane and orchestrates agent systems. RayDE is a client and a tool/context provider; it does not embed an agent. nan8 defines the protocols RayDE speaks; RayDE depends on none of its own crates from nan8's side and nan8 depends on none of RayDE's.\n- Sandbox API (nan8 docs/sandbox-api.md, draft v0): clients state requirements, nan8 places on MSB or dynASB and refuses with unsatisfiable rather than dropping a requirement; HTTPS plus WebSocket; events resumable.\n- Reflow carries messaging between native actors, dynASB and MSB, and is run as a standalone app server nan8 reads and writes graphs to. dynASB replaces Reflow's remote script actors; closing that layer is dynASB 9139bd7 (binary stream path landed locally in dynASB).\n- The GPU session class serves streaming previews and open-weight model serving (RayDE 48bab1d scope). Entitlement groundwork: native/sync Entitlement.gpu_ms_per_period and admit() (RayDE 5abd43d).\n- AEL is the agent loop (goals, plans, policy, verification). Its boundary to the world is typed effects, not a network service; a host embeds its runtime and registers a handler per effect.\n- HGM is the memory service, built on KyuGraph (hierarchical memory: semantic, episodic, procedural, emotional; temperature scoring; hot, warm and cold tiers; pattern graph). RayDE serves editor state into it as a knowledge graph with hierarchical memory. AEL's KyuGraph skill discovery stays a rebuildable projection; AEL keeps authority over its world.\n\nLayering\nAEL (what to do next, plan policy, verification) -\u003e nan8 (effect handlers, placement, sandboxes, metering, secrets, egress, tenancy, streams) -\u003e Reflow (messages between actors) -\u003e dynASB (GPU, actors) and MSB (allowlists, volumes, snapshots).\nRayDE: agent panel as a client of nan8's projection of the AEL world; IDE capabilities as effects (tool server, MCP, aab3b7c); human approval and authoring of plan rules; editor-state producer for HGM.\n\nEffects the host registers (each with a stable EffectId that maps to dynASB idempotency_key, run_id, attempt; pending handles map to resumable streams)\n- sandbox create, exec, snapshot: nan8 sandbox API\n- actor send and subscribe: Reflow and dynASB\n- deliberate: a model actor on the GPU pool, or an external provider through nan8 egress\n- memory read and write: HGM\n- ide read, edit, build, run: RayDE tool server\n- human approval: RayDE UI\n\nPolicy layers\nAEL rules decide whether an agent may act; nan8 enforces runtime limits (isolation, egress, quotas); RayDE grants gate workspace access and what may leave the session. Any layer can deny; none grants what another denies.\n\nOpen (darmie to decide)\n1. Who hosts the AEL runtime: embedded in nan8 (brings Zyntax's JIT into nan8's binary) or a small host process nan8 starts (recommended).\n2. Stream addressing per function or per sandbox (dynASB streams).\n3. Graceful guest shutdown on Linux: ask the guest, SIGTERM, or keep SIGKILL (recommended); the shutdown eventfd does not exist on x86_64 Linux in libkrun 1.19.7 (dynASB 472aa93).\n4. HGM tenancy and the code-specific memory labels and provenance fields the editor needs.\n5. Whether the agent protocol between RayDE and nan8 rides MCP or is its own.\n6. Pricing: GPU allowance per plan, and whether inference and rendering share it.\n\nWork items by repo\n- RayDE: tool server (aab3b7c), agent panel client, nan8 provider client (5640c6f), editor-state producer for HGM.\n- nan8: AEL host and effect handlers, durable journal storage adapter (S3, per-tenant), AEL world projection as events, scheduler (6cea173), sandbox API (3f71695), data plane (fb18741).\n- dynASB: 9139bd7 (Reflow layer), 472aa93, bbeeee0 (sandbox adapter, after the protocol settles), GPU tenant lifecycle (74889e9).\n- HGM: KyuGraph backing, tenant boundary, editor-state schema and labels.\n- AEL: durable storage adapter and a read-only world projection the host can publish.","files":null}]}